WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.240
Welcome to the Continuum setup.

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:04.400
Step one is actually the easy one.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.560
We're just going to find your old conversations.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:07.760
And you don't need to worry

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.680
about copying and pasting anything.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.840
The service you've been using can actually hand you

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.200
your entire history, all in just one single download.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.080
Now, that download is what we call an export.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.160
Basically, it's just a safe copy of the

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.320
history that your account makes available to you.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.520
Requesting this export doesn't move or remove a single

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.240
thing in your account, so you're totally safe there.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.640
Inside that download, you'll usually find

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:34.000
one specific file named conversations.json.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.920
That right there is your whole history.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:38.720
Every chat, every message perfectly in order.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.600
And that's exactly the file that Continuum reads.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.840
Getting this file is really straightforward.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.040
If you're using ChatGPT, you'll want to open your settings,

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.640
then head over to Data Controls, and click Export Data.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.080
Just confirm that, and then wait

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:53.600
for an email with your link.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.360
Over in Claude, it's pretty similar.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:58.560
Go to Settings, then Privacy, and then Export Data.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.240
Again, you'll get a link sent to you by email.

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:02.670
Oh, and if a workplace manages your account

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:04.510
and you don't see that option, no worries,

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:06.670
your administrator can actually grab that for you.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:08.910
When the download does arrive, it usually comes

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:10.750
as a zip file, which is really just

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:12.830
a few files cleanly packaged together.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:14.350
Go ahead and open it up, but

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:16.110
make sure to keep those files together.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:17.870
Our setup assistant is going to help you

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:20.190
pick the right conversation file and just double

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:21.390
check that it can be used.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:22.350
The best part?

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:23.790
You never actually need to read

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:25.870
or edit anything inside it yourself.

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:27.710
Just one more thing to keep in mind.

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:29.710
The download might not arrive right away

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:31.870
in your inbox, and that's completely normal.

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:34.030
You can absolutely just pause right here and

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:35.710
come back to this whenever it's ready.

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:37.870
Your account and all your original files will

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:40.190
stay exactly as they are while you wait.

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:41.870
So do you have your files already,

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:43.390
or would you like help getting them?

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:45.150
Press a button below.
